Changelog: 21-11-2026 19:56:43

Release 4.7.1.

Changelog: 21-11-2026 19:37:41

Fixed. The wiki chapter's part on the BIOS follows the suite's rule (owner, 21-11-2026): its main heading is The stock
P5.00 BIOS, with Disabling the IOMMU and Optional: ACPI fix under it. A custom BIOS is named once, as another route
that is not part of the suite. The Requirements section said the script's --all installs everything: it leaves out the
development extras, and it also installs mprime.

Changelog: 21-11-2026 18:54:58

Fixed. The app's text is rewritten to the writing standard: short sentences with one fact each, no chains with
semicolons, colons or long parentheses, plain American English and the purpose first. This covers the wiki chapter
(docs/apps/check.md), the README, the messages test-board.sh prints (results, hints, notes and the advice on journal
lines), the fake engine's copies of them, install-requirements.sh, two of install.sh's own messages and three test
descriptions in catalog.py. Lines the app parses keep their format, and a hint that spans several lines still joins into
one hint. No label was renamed. The engine's hints for the GUI now say to check a box instead of tick, and "restart"
instead of "reboot" outside commands. The README and a hint of tests 40 and 47 say wiki instead of manual. Facts
corrected: the wiki said Run all tests runs tests 00-40, and it runs every test except 42, 43 and 44, with 41 only when
its box is checked. Test 31 was described as verifying that /var/log exists and is writable, and it lists the folder and
verifies that it exists. The wiki named the graph button Save as PNG, and the window shows Save as PNG…. Nothing the app
does has changed. Tests changed: test_log_advice.py asserts the new wording of the two hints on failed units and
unexplained lines, and test_smoke.py looks for the chapter's new first words. Thirty names of programs and terms
the texts use were added to tools/text_check/words.txt.

